## Static red basis (why the test fails on the pre-change tree)

1. **Headline counts.** The test parses
   `Of **N tracked items** — ... **D are done**, P are partial, B are blocked ... **U were never started**.`
   and compares with `verification/requirements.json`:
   - inventory: 317 items, 227 normative, 90 acceptance, **18 DONE / 252 PARTIAL / 3 BLOCKED / 44 NOT_RUN**;
   - committed `verification/FINAL-REPORT.md:8`: **12 done / 250 partial / 4 blocked / 51 never started**.
   `assert.equal(Number(match[4]), totals.DONE)` fails (12 !== 18), and match[6]/match[7] fail too.
2. **Family rows.** The inventory has 21 families; e.g. `TOOL` is 2/3/1/0 in the inventory but
   the committed report shows `TOOL | 0 | 4 | 1 | 1` (FINAL-REPORT.md:95), and `DEC` is
   2/3/0/3 there but 0/1/1/6 in the committed table.
3. **DONE list.** The committed report omits DEC-01, DEC-02, RUN-04, TOOL-04, TOOL-05 and
   MOD-13 from "The requirements that are done" (FINAL-REPORT.md:29-40), while the inventory
   marks all six DONE.
4. **Timestamp/commit.** The committed report has no `**Generated** <ISO> from commit \`<sha>\``
   line at all, so the timestamp assertion fails.
5. **Package identities.** The committed report hardcodes "Five packages are published and
   installable" with `0.1.3` (FINAL-REPORT.md:18); the test requires every
   `packages/*/package.json` name+version (14 packages, host `0.5.42`, laya `1.0.3`, …) to
   appear in a generated table.
6. **Byte equality / `--check`.** The test asserts the file equals `renderFinalReport()` and
   that `node scripts/gen-final-report.mjs --check` exits 0. Before this change the
   generator has no `--check` mode (it always writes), so that case could not pass.

Green requires: implementation of the generator changes, a regenerated
`verification/FINAL-REPORT.md`, and the two commands run in a working shell.

